ers sent, rentals added, bookings confirmed, conversion, booked revenue and follow-ups due. Press <b class="gd-ui">By month</b> for months, <b class="gd-ui">By week</b> for weeks.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">By week (or By month) lists each period with the same figures, newest first.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Follow-ups due lists your open deals with what to do next: send the offer, follow up before the offer expires, or follow up while the renter signs and pays. Red means it is past due.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Deals lists every booking you created, added or sent an offer on in the last 180 days, with its status and what it counts. Open a request, an offer or a rental you added from its number.</div></li></ol></div><div class="gd-tablewrap"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Figure</th><th scope="col">How it is counted</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Credited to you</td><td>A quote you created, a rental you added, or a website request whose first offer you sent. An Admin can give a deal to someone else.</td></tr><tr><td>Quotes created, offers sent, rentals added</td><td>Counted on the day they happened.</td></tr><tr><td>Bookings confirmed, booked revenue</td><td>Counted on the day the booking was confirmed.</td></tr><tr><td>Conversion</td><td>Of the deals credited to you in the period, the share confirmed so far.</td></tr><tr><td>Booked revenue</td><td>The rental charge before tax, after discounts. A cancelled booking counts only what was kept; refunds come off.</td></tr><tr><td>Rental days (Sales)</td><td>The days of the completed, paid rentals you sourced that end in the month. The month&#39;s tier applies to all of that month&#39;s rentals.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Sales commissions are approved after the month ends, when the month&#39;s tier is known. A refund that drops the month under a tier lowers every commission of that month; anything already paid comes off your next payment.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="sales-owners-you-bring-in" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Owners you bring in</h2><p class="gd-p">Bring in car owners on <b class="gd-ui">My work</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">My sales</b>, card <b class="gd-ui">Owners you bring in</b>. Every owner you bring in is credited to you as &quot;sourced by&quot;, with their cars. Only an Admin can change that later.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Invite an owner</b>: enter their name, email and phone, tick <b class="gd-ui">The owner asked me to send it</b>, then press <b class="gd-ui">Send the invitation</b>. They get an email with your link to apply.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Copy my owner link</b>: your own link to the application, for a message or a post. Anyone who applies with it is credited to you.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Start an application</b>: you fill in the owner and the car for them, with <b class="gd-ui">Take a photo</b> (or <b class="gd-ui">Choose a photo</b>) of the ownership permit to fill in the car. It goes to an Admin as an application to approve. The terms and invoices are the Admin&#39;s.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">The row of five figures follows your owners: <b class="gd-ui">Invited</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Applied</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Approved</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Car live</b> and <b class="gd-ui">First paid rental</b>. Below, each owner shows their stage and their cars.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>An owner already on file, or invited first by another salesperson, cannot be invited again. Ask an Admin if you brought them in.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="sales-ask-for-your-commission-on-an-owner" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Ask for your commission on an owner</h2><p class="gd-p">There is no set amount. For each owner you bring in, you ask for one, and an Admin decides.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On the owner&#39;s row press <b class="gd-ui">Ask for a commission</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Choose <b class="gd-ui">A flat amount</b> and type it, or <b class="gd-ui">A percent</b>: type the percent, choose what it is of (the company&#39;s share of their cars&#39; rentals, or their cars&#39; rental revenue) and for how long (a number of months, or as long as the car is with us).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Add a note for the Admin if you like, then press <b class="gd-ui">Send to an Admin</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">While it waits you can press <b class="gd-ui">Change my request</b>. Once an Admin approves, changes or declines it, the row says so, with their note.</div></li></ol></div><div class="gd-tablewrap"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Approved as</th><th scope="col">When it is earned</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>A flat amount</td><td>Once, at the owner&#39;s first paid rental: the first completed rental of any of their cars, paid in full</td></tr><tr><td>A percent</td><td>On each completed, paid rental of their cars that ends after the approval, from the month of the first one, for the months approved</td></tr></tbody></table></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Nothing is earned before an Admin approves the request, and nothing on CarmaCars&#39; own cars, a partner&#39;s, a shareholder&#39;s or your own. Each commission then goes through the usual steps on My sales: pending approval, approved, paid.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="sales-owner-leads" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Owner leads</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Owner leads: each enquiry with the name, contact, car and status.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Take it</b> to make it yours, then call the owner.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Update</b> to set the status. When you close a lead, say why.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Owner applications, last 90 days, shows who applied and how far onboarding has come.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va/leads</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1230/400"><img src="/guides/img/va-sales-04-leads-desktop-3402e913.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1230" height="400"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:6.5%;top:26.5%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:94.8%;top:44%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:15.4%;top:63%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="sales-owner-pipeline" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Owner pipeline</h2><p class="gd-p">Open <b class="gd-ui">Owner pipeline</b> (Sales or Customer service). Every prospective owner is a card in its stage: New, Contacted, Call booked, Agreement sent, Signed, Car onboarded or Lost.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Follow-up emails go by themselves on day 0, 2, 5 and 10 and stop when the lead replies or you move the card.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">After you talk to them, press <b class="gd-ui">Move</b> and choose the stage. Add a note; when lost, say why.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">They answered by email? Press <b class="gd-ui">They replied</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Add an owner lead</b> for someone who called or walked in, or who was referred (a referral gets one email only).</div></li></ol></div></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('va', 'commissions', 'chapter', 'add-a-rental-by-hand', 'Every function earns a commission on the rentals it sources: a renter you found yourself. Say so when you enter the rental, the quote or the offer.

## Mark who found the client

Every rental, quote and offer you enter asks: **I sourced this client** or **Entered for CarmaCars**.

1. Choose **I sourced this client** when you found the renter yourself: someone you know, your own post or your own outreach.
2. Choose **Entered for CarmaCars** when the renter came to CarmaCars: the website, the phone line, a walk-in, a partner.
3. A website request earns nothing by itself. If you sourced it anyway, choose I sourced this client on its offer: an Admin decides.

|  | Commission |
| --- | --- |
| Sales | Commission only, with no base pay. By the rental days of the month, on all of that month''s rentals: in person under 50 days 10%, from 50 days 15%, from 100 days 20%; remote 5%, 10% and 15%, one tier lower in a month under 400 touches (chapter Sales) |
| Customer service, finance, fleet | 10% |
| How much | The rate on the rental charge before tax, after discounts, with late extra days; never on delivery, kilometres, add-ons or anything else bought. Only a refund of the rental charge comes off |
| When earned | When the rental is completed and paid in full. Never on a cancelled, refunded, unpaid or charged-back rental, or on your own or a household rental |
| Your home address | It must be in your profile. Until it is, a commission waits as not earned yet, and you cannot add a rental or mark I sourced this client |
| Paid | After an Admin approves it, by transfer or on your pay statement. My sales shows each step: not earned yet, pending approval, approved, paid, reversed |

> Tip: A refund or chargeback after a commission was paid comes off your next payment. Your staff agreement has the full rule.
', 'Commissions', 'I sourced this client, your rate, when it is earned, approved and paid.',
